{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3055","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3055","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3055\",\"parent_revision\":\"33986b501f7d765f83d73aa9ae489cf8690bfe995103e55314bd1e1bda0e483a\",\"root_revision\":\"33986b501f7d765f83d73aa9ae489cf8690bfe995103e55314bd1e1bda0e483a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nArtifacts registered against an item can report `status: \\\"current\\\"` with `storage_tier: \\\"remote\\\"` in the manifest while their content cannot be retrieved. The manifest and the content store disagree, and the disagreement surfaces only when a read is attempted.\\n\\nReproduced against item #2529, which lists eight registered artifacts, all `status: \\\"current\\\"`:\\n\\n```text\\nartifact_list(item_id=2529)\\n  -> 8 artifacts, every one status=\\\"current\\\", storage_tier=\\\"remote\\\"\\n\\nartifact_read(item_id=2529, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")\\n  -> Error: Content was not found: {\\\"kind\\\":\\\"artifact_content\\\",\\\"namespace\\\":\\\"2529\\\",\\n     \\\"artifact_type\\\":\\\"architect\\\",\\n     \\\"name\\\":\\\"plan/architect-recursive-sub-section-and-code-fence-navigation-for-backlog-view.md\\\"}\\n\\nartifact_read(item_id=2529, artifact_type=\\\"feature-context\\\")\\n  -> Error: Content was not found: (same shape)\\n```\\n\\nBlast radius is unverified. Item #2529 is confirmed affected across at least two artifact types. Whether this is item-specific, provider-specific, type-specific, or systemic has not been established \u2014 a second item checked (#2956) has no artifacts registered, so it provided no contrast.\\n\\n### Why this matters beyond the single item\\n\\nThe affected artifacts are the authoritative architecture record for the progressive-disclosure subsystem. `docs/mcp-progressive-disclosure-contract.md` explicitly defers its design rationale to the `architect` artifact on #2529 \u2014 so the reasoning behind currently-shipping behaviour is unreachable, and design questions about that subsystem cannot be settled from the repository record.\\n\\nThe intended architecture (see `docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`, R6) places the artifact inventory on the default item-view response path. Once that lands, artifact retrieval stops being an incidental call and becomes part of the primary read path \u2014 an unreadable-artifact failure would then surface on ordinary item views rather than only when something explicitly asks for one.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Root cause established: why a manifest entry can report `current` while the content store has no matching record\\n- [ ] Blast radius measured: how many registered artifacts across how many items are currently unreadable\\n- [ ] The manifest and content store cannot disagree silently \u2014 a registered-but-unreadable artifact is detectable without attempting a read, or the read failure carries enough detail to distinguish \\\"never stored\\\" from \\\"stored and lost\\\"\\n- [ ] Recovery decision recorded for artifacts whose content is unrecoverable \u2014 whether the manifest entry is corrected, marked, or removed\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs an **agent retrieving a report or asset associated with a backlog item**, I want **a registered artifact's content to be readable** so that **the design records and analyses produced during grooming remain accessible to the work that depends on them**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Discovered while tracing the progressive-disclosure design record, 2026-08-20\\n- **Priority**: P1 \u2014 blocks retrieval of design records now; moves onto the primary read path under the intended architecture\\n- **Related**: #3054 (architecture refresh), #3050 (undefined ADRs \u2014 same pattern of design rationale being unreachable)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"9b7d15a53a133eb1890c319f06da632df763c74ce332dc55ca3ae5d86d01bd0b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvbuCw\"}"}